# 13. Extract Source IP Addresses

Try:

```bash
grep "Failed password" security-events.log | awk '{print $(NF-3)}'
```

Then:

```bash
grep "Failed password" security-events.log | awk '{print $(NF-3)}' | sort | uniq -c
```

Expected concept:

```text
5 192.168.1.50
```

This tells us that the same source IP generated five authentication failures in the sample data.

> Log formats differ between systems, so `awk` field positions must always be verified against the actual log format.

